  "final_message": "Everything builds and passes end-to-end checks. Summary of what was implemented:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- SQLite at `./data/billing.db` (WAL-safe, created on startup)\n- Auth: register (201), login \u2192 bearer token (200), token-authenticated `/api/me` and logout\n- Subscriptions CRUD with `q`/`status`/`plan`/`page`/`page_size` filtering, newest first\n- Invoices (issue open invoice, newest-first history)\n- Collections: `failed` increments failure count and moves active\u2192past_due; `succeeded` pays open invoices, resets failures, restores past_due\u2192active\n- Public stats with MRR (active + past_due only) and per-status counts\n- Money rounded to 2 decimals; health endpoint; SPA fallback serving `frontend/dist`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4)\n- Auth forms, signed-in username + sign-out\n- Public MRR/status-cards page\n- Subscription table with status tabs, plan filter, debounced customer search, paging, create form\n- Subscription detail with edit form, invoice history, issue-invoice form, and success/failure collection buttons\n\nVerified: `npm run build`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, and a full API exercise (auth, filters, paging, CRUD, invoices, collections, stats, SPA routing) all pass. Note: Docker isn't available in this sandbox, so image build couldn't be run locally, but no Dockerfile changes were needed.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
